---
version: 2.0.2
title: lex diagnostic: unexpected characters
file: ./test/lexer_snapshot_test.gleam
test_name: unexpected_characters_diagnostic_test
---
Source:
module main

main() {
  let a = 'x'
  let b = “quoted”
  let c = a ^ b
  let d = ~a
  let e = #x
  let f = café @@
}

---
error: single-quoted string
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:4:11
  │
4 │   let a = 'x'
  │           ─┬─
  │            ╰─ strings use double quotes
  ╰─

Write `"x"` instead.

note: Pooka has no separate character type.

error: typographic quotes
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:5:11
  │
5 │   let b = “quoted”
  │           ────┬───
  │               ╰─ these are typographic quotes
  ╰─

Strings are written with plain double quotes: `"quoted"`.

error: unexpected character
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:6:13
  │
6 │   let c = a ^ b
  │             ┬
  │             ╰─ this cannot start any Pooka syntax
  ╰─

`^` is not valid here.

error: unexpected character
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:7:11
  │
7 │   let d = ~a
  │           ┬
  │           ╰─ this cannot start any Pooka syntax
  ╰─

`~` is not valid here.

error: unexpected `#`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:8:11
  │
8 │   let e = #x
  │           ┬
  │           ╰─ `#` must be followed by `(`
  ╰─

Tuples are written `#(first, second)`.

error: unexpected character
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:9:14
  │
9 │   let f = café @@
  │              ┬
  │              ╰─ not valid outside strings and comments
  ╰─

`é` cannot be used here.

note: Names may only contain ASCII letters, digits and underscores.

error: unexpected characters
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:9:16
  │
9 │   let f = café @@
  │                ─┬
  │                 ╰─ this cannot start any Pooka syntax
  ╰─

`@@` is not valid here.

Found 7 errors.

